    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d996">

                <pb facs="0872" n="756" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg756"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/3348.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Consul at
                            Chihuahua to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Chihuahua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">via El
                                Paso, Tex.</hi>)</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1912-03-22T15:00:00-07:04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 22, 1912—3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>There are press reports of prohibition entry foodstuffs through Paso del Norte,
                    which will cause much bitterness toward Americans. In this event mines can not
                    continue beyond two weeks at any rate, and so think better close at once and
                    Americans withdraw. It seems to me that such action coupled with strict
                    enforcement the President’s proclamation will effectively stifle the revolution.
                    Unless <pb facs="0873" n="757" xml:id="pg757"/> otherwise instructed will
                    counsel withdrawal Americans and closing mines immediately upon notice of the
                    President’s approval of action prohibiting exportation food through Paso del
                    Norte.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Letcher.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
